-> Test: native module emission — FireLog handler emits a Log particle received by a handler.
link native_modules/libtest_helper.so as helper

-> Define local handler for emitted Log particles. No local schema
-> declaration needed — handler dispatch is purely _class-based (T30);
-> the native module's own "Log" type (source/level/message) is already
-> registered at the qualified `helper.Log`, used below for the return.
-> The native module emits Log{source, level, message} with _class = "Log".
Log => {
    assert source = "test_helper"
    assert level = "Info"
    assert message = "hello from native"
    return helper.Log { source = source, level = level, message = message }
}

-> Invoking FireLog handler should emit a Log particle which our handler catches.
req = helper.FireLog { message = "hello from native" }
emit req to helper get _
